{"archetypes":[{"name":"line-ref-verifier","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan stakes its entire invariant argument on ~10 specific line-number claims in implement-bootstrap.sh (dirty-tree checkpoint at ~750 as the FIRST post-skip helper, create-branch.sh at ~765, phase_tracking early-return at 540-582, and four more); if any are stale the audit prose and grep pins will document the wrong ordering and the correctness argument collapses.","prompt_body":"Cross-check every specific line-number or line-range claim in the plan against the actual current content of scripts/implement-bootstrap.sh: confirm that run_dirty_tree_checkpoint is the FIRST call after the resume-skip block and that the resume-skip block ends before line 749, verify that create-branch.sh appears near line 765 and that the phase_tracking RESUME_PLAN_TAIL early-return spans lines 540-582, and check that the five remaining helpers (git-current-branch.sh, run-step1-plan-log.sh, write-tally.sh, tracking-issue-summary.sh upsert-summary, and phase_tracking itself) fall near their claimed line numbers. Also verify that the existing assertions near lines 419-424 of scripts/test-implement-structure.sh use the grep -Fq style the plan says the new pins will mirror, so the style claim is accurate. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
